    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. it's more than just \"emotional connection\" though. when i see these words, it feels like they are specifically designed to bypass the critical thinking part of the brain. like they are \"resetting\" your mental state to be more suggestible. if we look at the structure—the way they use these high-vibration, vague promises—is there a pattern there that suggests they aren't just selling a product, but actually installing a specific mindset? like a way to make people stop questioning the status quo?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
